# =====================================================================
# This repo is shared on GitHub for the ①ESP32 and ④web modules ONLY.
# ②rpi5/ and ③cloud/ are a local reference implementation the teammate
# owning those modules is replacing with their own — excluded below so
# they never get committed. See INTEGRATION.md for the contract their
# replacement needs to satisfy (what ESP32 sends it, what it must send web/).
#
# Local-only dev tooling (assumes the excluded rpi5/ is present, so it's
# useless to a fresh clone that only has esp32/+web/) is excluded too —
# see SETUP.md for what a teammate actually needs after cloning.
# All patterns below are anchored to the repo root (leading "/") so they
# never accidentally match a same-named path nested inside esp32/ or web/
# (e.g. esp32/scripts/ must NOT be excluded by the root /scripts/ rule).
# =====================================================================
/rpi5/
/cloud/
/run.bat
/test.bat
/stop.bat
/scripts/
/HOW_TO_RUN.md
/PORTING_CHECKLIST.md

# Repo scope kept minimal: only esp32/, web/, and the two teammate-facing
# setup docs (SETUP.md, INTEGRATION.md) go to GitHub. These are local-only.
/README.md
/DESIGN.md
/claude_code_prompt.md
/docs/

# Edge Impulse SDK (~24MB, vendored from a zip export) — too big for the repo.
# Teammates re-install it after cloning: see SETUP.md / esp32/scripts/install_ei_model.py.
esp32/lib/
# The downloaded EI export zip itself (dropped at repo root to run the install
# script against) — also shouldn't be committed, same reason.
/*.zip

# Python (kept in case rpi5/cloud exclusion above is ever lifted)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
web/.env

# Per-user secrets (Wi-Fi, ...) — copy from the matching .example
esp32/include/config.h

# ESP32 / PlatformIO
esp32/.pio/

# Misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
